title: Local runtime and independent acceptance boundary
query: >-
  Use the current PR head's referenced implementation as the runtime authority;
  historical diagrams and generated snapshots are compatibility evidence only.
  Show Docker wrapping exactly two independently built application images as
  Compose containers. Nest NGINX and its static assets inside the frontend
  container, and the Fastify factory, scoped upload plugin, sibling health
  plugin, instance lifecycle, native server adapter and pure parser inside one
  Node process in the API container. Show root TypeBox schemas and canonical
  errors, dynamic Swagger registered before features, upload onRequest admission
  before allocation, bounded collection and terminal cleanup. Successful API
  requests enter Fastify. The native adapter retains raw path/method/Expect
  refusals and finite documentation serving before Fastify dispatch. Production
  readiness loads verified docs before listening; close hooks own bounded
  shutdown. Put both containers inside Docker's Compose network. Keep browser
  React page components, useMp3Analysis business state and the raw Ky API
  service outside Docker, with the host controller and extracted Playwright
  runner also outside Docker. App.tsx composes the page; Vite builds static
  assets. The API image also packages the locally generated Redoc HTML, OpenAPI
  specification and renderer assets. Show build-only generation from createApp,
  ready, swagger and close outside the runtime services. Its finite docs adapter
  serves these assets after readiness; Redoc executes in the browser, not Node.
  Generation alone does not establish browser/CSP evidence. NGINX proxies /docs/
  and its specification/assets to the same private API with the untouched
  request URI and docs-scoped public CSP. All documentation assets are
  same-origin, with no CDN or additional runtime service. Distinguish published
  loopback host port from internal frontend port 8080 and private API port 3000,
  with a separate test-only loopback binding for direct API diagnostics. Show
  source-defined runtime users, read-only filesystems, temporary mounts and
  bounded in-process parsing. Do not imply a third parser/test container, Node
  frontend runtime or cloud deployment. Keep fixed API lifecycle readback and
  SIGTERM inside the host controller; command acknowledgment does not prove
  graceful drain.
